CWEs: CWE-89 (Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection') - Medium Confidence, CWE-256 (Unprotected Storage of Credentials) - High Confidence, CWE-502 (Deserialization of Untrusted Data) - Low Confidence, CWE-731 (Improper Validation of Object References) - Medium Confidence, CWE-200 (Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor) - High Confidence
</analysis>

