 <analysis>
This code contains one potential security vulnerability. The function `user_locations()` is susceptible to XPath Injection attacks due to the concatenation of user input (username) directly into the XPath query string without any sanitisation or parameterisation. An attacker could manipulate the username parameter with malicious XPath expressions to access arbitrary data within the XML file.

Here's an example of how an attacker might abuse this vulnerability:
```
/users/user[1]/location  // This would return the location of the first user in the XML file, instead of the intended user.
/users/user[position()=2+1]/location  // This would return the location of the second user in the XML file. The attacker could potentially use this to enumerate users if there's a limit on the number of requests allowed.
```
In order to mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to parameterize the XPath query by using functions like `ET.XPathEval()` or using safer libraries that handle user input more securely.
</analysis>

