<analysis>
The provided code contains a potential security vulnerability. The function `filterScriptTags` uses the `re.sub` function to remove `<script>` tags from the input content. However, using regular expressions for this purpose can be risky because it is prone to various edge cases and may not correctly handle all types of malicious script injection.

One such issue arises when dealing with nested or malformed HTML/XML content. The regular expression used (`r'<script.*?>.*?</script>'`) assumes that the `<script>` tag is well-formed and does not account for potential issues like comments within the script tags or unclosed tags.

Additionally, using a greedy match (`.*?`) can lead to unintended removal of parts of the HTML content if the script tag contains characters that are also valid in other parts of the content.

