The severity of this vulnerability is high because it can allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the server, leading to potential server compromise or denial of service.

Additionally, there are no checks to ensure that the `pattern` or `text` inputs are properly formatted and do not contain any malicious content. This could lead to other types of attacks, such as cross-site scripting (XSS) if the inputs are reflected back in the response.

