CWEs: CWE-79 (Cross-site Scripting) - Moderate Confidence

The confidence level is "Moderate" because while there are clear issues with the regex's comprehensiveness, this code does not directly expose data and relies on additional security layers to be completely secure. The identified vulnerability primarily relates to inadequacy in script filtering rather than an outright exploitable flaw.

