2025-10-29 18:41:15,527 - Logger.LLMEval - DEBUG - debug:143 - Response from deepseek-coder:6.7b for sample 35:
<analysis>
The server_bad function is using Python's built-in traceback module to catch all exceptions, including those thrown by do_computation(). The try and except block will catch any exception, not just those that can be handled in the application. This means that even if an error occurs within do_computation(), it would still be caught here, leading to potential data leakage or server degradation.

Moreover, without a specific handler for exceptions thrown by do_computation(), the traceback information includes all preceding frames of the call stack - including code in flask itself which could potentially reveal sensitive implementation details about your Flask app if not handled correctly. 

This results in potential misuse of error handling and can lead to security vulnerabilities like Sensitive Data Exposure (CWE-200), where information that is usually kept confidential may be leaked due to improper exception handling.
</analysis>

